pillarium (1.0.3-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Add modal alert dialogs for three levels: startup (shown when
    Pillarium launches), warning and error.  Dialogs are centred,
    themed, keyboard driven (Esc dismisses, Enter/Space actuates the
    default button) and stack in a queue.
  * Add unresponsive-application detection via the _NET_WM_PING
    protocol; a window that stops replying raises an error alert
    offering Wait or Force Quit.
  * Route critical D-Bus notifications (urgency >= 2) to error alerts,
    leaving normal/low notifications on the existing toast.
  * Add the pillarium-notify(1) command so scripts and applications can
    raise an alert over a local UNIX socket.
  * Ship Ogg Vorbis alert chimes (startup/warn/error) under the package
    and play them through the first available PipeWire/PulseAudio/
    ffmpeg/mpv/vorbis-tools/SoX player, falling back to the terminal
    bell.  Sound, volume and per-level enablement are configurable in
    the new "alerts" section of config.json.

 -- Pillarium Developers <pillarium@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 16 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000

pillarium (1.0.2-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Add Ethernet (wired) support: a taskbar indicator that reflects the
    nmcli device state, and an Alt+Shift+E menu to connect/disconnect
    wired devices.
  * Add Alt+Tab / Alt+Shift+Tab window cycling between managed windows.
  * Add a live light/dark theme toggle (Alt+Shift+D) that repaints every
    frame, decoration, the taskbar, desktop icons and any open popup.
  * Reload config.json automatically when it changes on disk, so external
    editors (e.g. Planet Control Center) apply settings without a restart.
  * Clean shutdown: terminate the wallpaper/compositor helpers, close
    menus, the search bar, dialogs and notifications, destroy managed
    windows and the taskbar, and handle SIGTERM/SIGINT/SIGHUP.
  * Fix importing the package without dbus-python/gi installed: the
    D-Bus notification service is now defined only when D-Bus is
    available, and notifications are skipped gracefully otherwise.

