pillarium (1.0.0-3) unstable; urgency=low

  * Fix clicking on objects inside windows: the passive button grabs on
    managed clients used owner_events=True with an async pointer grab,
    so XAllowEvents(ReplayPointer) was a no-op and every press on a
    client window was swallowed by the window manager. The grabs now
    use owner_events=False with GrabModeSync (freezing the pointer at
    the press) and the button handler replays the press, so the
    application receives the click exactly as if the window manager
    had never intercepted it (click-to-focus without breaking clicks).
  * Add a replay safety net for presses that arrive while a client is
    being torn down, so the pointer is never left frozen.

 -- Pillarium Developers <pillarium@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 15 Aug 2026 22:00:00 +0000

pillarium (1.0.0-2) unstable; urgency=low

  * Fix minimise: hidden windows are kept alive (unmapped) instead of
    being destroyed, focus is released, and they can be restored from
    the taskbar.
  * Fix click-to-focus: clicks on a window's client area now activate
    the window via passive button grabs, replaying the click to the
    application so it still receives it.
  * Remove the subwindow event-mask rewriting that broke client event
    delivery (BadAccess on application-owned subwindows).
  * Clicking empty desktop space now drops keyboard focus.

